{
  "ranking": [
    { "id": "patch_12707f7188ea", "mechanism": "Condition (acc_reg >= rate_num) ignores that s_axis_tready depends on m_axis_tready_int_early and pause; gating by !s_axis_tready in line 118 reduces premature pause during backpressure, aligning s_axis_tready behavior at cycle 12." },
    { "id": "patch_28182ef789d2", "mechanism": "Registering store_axis_temp_to_output using m_axis_tvalid_next (line 199) ensures the temp register valid flag matches the scheduled output valid, preventing the m_axis_tvalid glitch at cycle 8 and cycle 15." },
    { "id": "patch_3732446a2223", "mechanism": "At reset the initial m_axis_tvalid_reg is 1'b0, but s_axis_tvalid drives m_axis_tvalid_int; assigning s_axis_tvalid to m_axis_tvalid_reg (line 252) seeds the output pipeline with the first input valid, fixing the early m_axis_tvalid mismatch at cycle 8." },
    { "id": "patch_e6e9f736fdb3", "mechanism": "Assigning m_axis_tkeep (width KEEP_WIDTH) to s_axis_tready_reg (line 155) is a width/substitution error; however the diff is in the reset/initial block and the simulator reads s_axis_tready_reg from the always_ff block, so the practical effect is seeding s_axis_tready_reg from the rate logic instead of 0, which shifts the first ready pulse and alters s_axis_tready at cycle 12." },
    { "id": "patch_fd49deeec05e", "mechanism": "Adding !rate_by_frame to the pause condition (line 128) stops frame-independent pause when rate_by_frame=1, preventing the spurious s_axis_tready deassertion at cycle 12 seen in the trace where rate_by_frame=1." },
    { "id": "patch_5eb30d5685b3", "mechanism": "Assigning m_axis_tready to s_axis_tready_reg (line 155) directly feeds the downstream ready into the upstream ready register, collapsing the skid-buffer handshake timing and moving the first s_axis_tready assertion, which matches the cycle-12 mismatch." },
    { "id": "patch_413743f5dfd2", "mechanism": "Qualifying the m_axis_tready_int_reg handshake gate with !rst (line 201) prevents the skid-buffer state machine from advancing during reset, keeping m_axis_tvalid_reg at 0 until the first post-reset cycle and fixing the m_axis_tvalid glitch at cycle 8." },
    { "id": "patch_70ab4c75caf9", "mechanism": "Driving m_axis_tready_int_reg from m_axis_tready (line 253) replaces the combinational early-ready with the registered downstream ready, changing the skid-buffer push timing and affecting both m_axis_tvalid (cycle 8) and s_axis_tready (cycle 12)." }
  ],
  "explanation": "The trace shows three primary deviations: m_axis_tvalid is 0 at cycle 8 (expected 1), s_axis_tready is 1 at cycle 12 (expected 0), and m_axis_tdata/m_axis_tuser shift starting cycle 13. The first two are handshake/startup issues; the data shift is a consequence of the altered handshake timing. Patches that reseed or gate the valid/ready registers during the first post-reset cycles (patch_3732446a2223, patch_413743f5dfd2, patch_28182ef789d2, patch_70ab4c75caf9) directly address the cycle-8 valid error. Patches that modify the pause/ready combinational logic (patch_12707f7188ea, patch_fd49deeec05e, patch_e6e9f736fdb3, patch_5eb30d5685b3) directly address the cycle-12 ready error. Structural-coverage is uniformly 1.0, so ranking follows failure-anchor proximity and mechanism specificity to the two key mismatches."
}
